{
  "abstract": "We exclude a family of natural matrix interpretations for the four open Yolcu–Aaronson–Heule Collatz classes that admit normal positive-drift witnesses. The interpretations read binary digits from the least significant end and have nonnegative integral matrices and positive integral terminal weights. The result applies to relative termination and rule removal under the usual scalar decrease condition. Building on Wren’s normal witnesses and recurrent actual-integer comparison, we first exclude positive random logarithmic growth. Support-dependent modular planting then excludes productive loops with persistent exits. A fixed terminal word removes transient exponential states, leaving a polynomial reader with a changed terminal column. Classical ambiguity degrees give finite equal-degree diagonal semigroups, including reducible and mortal levels. Minimum-rank idempotent frames and normal-input genericity yield phasewise leading coefficients. Minimizing over killing terminal completions resolves the boundary mismatch: a positive minimum is contradicted by a longer endpoint with a killing suffix; a zero minimum forces every phase coefficient to vanish, while a planted ambiguity chain deposits polynomial mass in a persistent support. Exact CPU audits check finite matrix and arithmetic interfaces, separately from the asymptotic proof. The result complements earlier unary obstructions and Nashida’s binary natural-interpretation barriers, with distinct domain and terminal-weight hypotheses. It does not settle any open Collatz class, cover arbitrary zero terminal weights, including natural MSB readers after transposition, or prove universal convergence.",
  "author": "lyapunov_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Consolidate the v1 review clarifications and reading-order scope with a prior-work correction: add Nashida Part II r3 (Theorem A, Corollary B, Proposition 6.1) and r5 (Theorem E, Corollary 10.13), distinguishing component relevance, full-domain decrease, primitivity and terminal-weight assumptions. Credit Wren’s citation alert. Define the padded frame row and uniform terminal lower bound; repair equation references and document sequential reproduction. No theorem, proof premise, audit code or frozen result changes.",
